# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Better Call Kanoon - ignore rules (REPOSITORY ROOT)
#
# Layout: `backend/` is the FastAPI app (Python), `frontend/` is the Vite +
# React + TypeScript client. This file covers BOTH sides - Python bytecode and
# virtualenvs on one, node_modules and build output on the other.
#
# Why the two rules that matter most are here:
#
#   1. backend/data/laws/*.pdf - the statute PDFs are downloaded by the user
#      from official sources such as the India Code portal. They are large,
#      they change when the Government of India republishes them, and committing
#      them would push copyrighted government material into the repository.
#      The `data/laws/` directory itself IS tracked (via its .gitkeep), so a
#      fresh clone still has somewhere to put them.
#
#   2. backend/data/index/* - the retrieval index (embeddings, chunk vectors,
#      BM25 postings) is a BUILD ARTEFACT. It is large, it is binary, and it
#      is fully reproducible from the law PDFs by running the ingestion script.
#      Committing it means every re-index creates a noisy diff. Only the
#      directory placeholder is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The backend's environment file is `backend/.env` (that is the directory
# pydantic-settings reads, and the file docker-compose.yml passes through).
# `backend/.env.example` is the only environment file that is tracked.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# --- User-supplied legal source material ------------------------------------
backend/data/laws/*.pdf
backend/data/laws/*.doc
backend/data/laws/*.docx

# --- Generated retrieval index (directory kept, contents ignored) -----------
backend/data/index/*
!backend/data/index/.gitkeep

# --- Runtime logs -----------------------------------------------------------
# Order matters, and so does the *shape* of the pattern:
#
#   * `backend/logs/*` (contents, not the directory) lets git descend into
#     backend/logs/ so the negation below can re-include the placeholder. A
#     bare `logs/` would match backend/logs/ at ANY depth, and git never
#     descends into an ignored directory - which would silently make
#     `backend/logs/.gitkeep` untrackable.
#   * `logs/*.log` is rooted at the repository root (a pattern containing a
#     slash is anchored), so it covers a root logs/ folder without touching
#     backend/logs/. `*.log` then catches log files anywhere.
backend/logs/*
logs/*.log
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
!backend/logs/.gitkeep

# --- Frontend (Vite + React + TypeScript) -----------------------------------
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
# Vite build output - a build artefact, served by the backend at runtime.
# `npm run build` in frontend/ regenerates it; it is never committed.
frontend/dist/
frontend/build/
# Vite caches and env files (the real .env.example stays tracked).
frontend/.vite/
frontend/.cache/
*.local

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# --- Virtual environments ---------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# --- Test / lint / type caches ----------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.tox/

# --- Editors and IDEs -------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.spyderproject
.ropeproject

# --- Operating system cruft -------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- OS / editor temp files -------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig

# --- Local uploads and scratch space ----------------------------------------
.cache/
tmp/
temp/